hi there good evening Steve Kaufman here  today I want to talk about writing  correction and I think I've talked about  it before but the subject has come up at  our forum at Linc and so I thought I  would would talk about it I was playing  golf this afternoon and I was thinking  about this whole issue of writing  correction there is increasing  realization the writing correction in  terms of improving the accuracy of the  student is largely ineffective and if  you google writing correction effective  you'll find lots of studies that that  have been done where they study people  who have the writing corrected and even  corrected in four different ways you  know with explanations or without  explanations colored pencils and and it  really doesn't seem to matter correcting  people writing has very little effect on  how accurately they use the language and  certainly that's been my experience  however I think writing correction can  be useful first of all if if I write  something say a link and I submit it for  correction I am gonna take a little more  care and I might look up some  grammatical tables maybe look up a word  in the dictionary to find out if it's  masculine or feminine or how to spell it  or something so the fact that it's going  to be corrected by someone maybe puts a  little more pressure on me and I think  the big part of writing for correction  is actually the fact that we are writing  like writing itself is a very good thing  to do because you're forced to think  think through what you want to say and  perhaps do a little bit of research and  all this time you're thinking about the  words and I think that is 90% of the  advantage of submitting something to be  corrected the actual correction you  receive has  relatively little impact I mean I know  in my own case I get the mistakes back  in fact and this is the second thing the  biggest advantage and I should say the  correcting writing is something that is  done throughout the school system it's a  major part of language instruction and  yet it is essentially quite useless but  what I find useful and first of all when  I was correcting people's English at  link by far the largest category of  mistakes because we had different  categories you know the singular plural  tenses prepositions articles and so  forth the biggest problem people had was  in what we called use of words in other  words it might be grammatically correct  but the biggest issue is they didn't put  the words together in a way that was  natural for the native speaker and when  I get when I got my corrected texts back  what was most interesting to me was how  the native speaker had reorganized the  words to make it sound more natural and  then I would save those phrases to  review so what I was more interested in  because you know getting the cases right  and all this stuff is just gradually  over time reviewing them maybe reading  listening writing slowly you know you'll  get better at it having it corrected for  you has relatively little impact however  seeing you know I put words together in  a certain way and that comes this  natural expression so that to me is very  significant and that's why I think that  writing correction should only be done  by a native speaker because only a  native speaker has a natural field for  how the words are put together and how  the words are used and what is a natural  expression a non-native speaker might  table the correct of tense or correct  you know it's singular or you know the  agreement in French or something that  but those things are essentially minor  and having them corrected he's not going  to have my  impact on you what I think we need to  get out of these the writing production  which which is but I look forward to is  how the words are put together natural  phrasing natural patterns that I can  then save and review and perhaps use so  so therefore writing correction should  be done by native speakers and yet the  overwhelming majority of writing  correction that is done in our schools  and so forth is done by non-native  speakers who will look for things that  they think they know that the student  doesn't know and mark them down on it  which is relatively unhelpful so there  you have it some thoughts on writing  correction I look forward to your views  bye for now
 

